  "name": "F12: combat pause agrees on both peers (Tidewake, surface wild)",
  "claim": "ACCEPTANCE F12 clause 'combat pause ... agree'. A swimmer (first the GUEST while the host watches, then the HOST while the guest watches) swims by stick from the rest_03 landing to the authored surface wild pair road_visibility_tidal_cradle_to_salt_crown_sheltered_04 and engages it with the Engage press. Baselines first: both views show HUMAN and the watcher sees the swimmer's stamina_fraction draining. Then (a) the swimmer's own swim mode and the watcher's view of it are COMBAT_PAUSED (3), sampled twice 60 frames apart with stamina_fraction unchanged, and the swimmer's own stamina and health frozen; (b) a mid-fight party_cycle press switches creatures and both views stay paused; (c) the wild is won through the production combat path; (d) both views return to HUMAN (1) and 120 frames later the watcher sees stamina_fraction falling again, while the swimmer's own drain matches the configured rate. Setup (disclosed): dock unlock flags set through the ledger as smoke_water_combat_pause does, a level-50 two-member Water party granted, the swimmer placed on the authored rest_03 dry landing, the enemy's hp capped at 12 for the win (the enemy_hp_ceiling allowance). Not claimed: an aggressive interception -- every Water wild site spawns with aggressive=false.",
